{"id":"4682a076-589e-4690-b81d-9cf4d1cf1c2d","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243702,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT r.order_id) / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id), 0), 2) AS refund_rate\nFROM orders o\nLEFT JOIN refunds r ON r.order_id = o.order_id\nWHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable');","reasoning_content":"We need answer SQL only. Need compute refund_rate per metric. Question asks overall refund rate. Need join orders refunds. Metric expression ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT r.order_id) / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id),0),2), filter o.order_status NOT IN canceled unavailable. Need ensure denominator all valid orders. If left join from orders to refunds, numerator distinct refunded order ids among valid orders; denominator all valid orders. Should we count refunds of any status or all refund records? Metric says refund orders / valid orders no status filter. Use refunds. We need only one row. Could use COUNT(DISTINCT r.order_id). Since orders unique. LEFT JOIN orders o LEFT JOIN refunds r ON. WHERE valid. But if refunds has order_id not in orders excluded. That's okay denominator valid orders and numerator refund orders among valid orders? Metric expression uses r and o same join. It counts distinct r.order_id from joined rows where o valid. So yes. SQL:\n\nSELECT ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT r.order_id) / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id), 0), 2) AS refund_rate\nFROM orders o\nLEFT JOIN refunds r ON r.order_id = o.order_id\nWHERE o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable');\n\nNeed no LIMIT? Aggregation single row no group by exempt. Could also output no comment. Need only SQL. Check rule: only SELECT, direct executable. Good.\n\nNeed consider if numerator should only include refund status? No metric not. Good.\n\nPotential issue refund status smallint includes rejected, pending. Refund订单数 could count any refund request; metric says refund